  "source_name": "https://www.whattoexpect.com/pregnancy/week-by-week/week-28.aspx",
  "source_type": "website",
  "structure": {
    "block_count": 89,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "28 Weeks Pregnant",
        "text_sha256": "9d2e335f37299c37c97a2b8c8f2dc32559089682cb23ead42f9304378df9df3c",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Your baby is as big as a head of lettuce.",
        "text_sha256": "15e2b75ef5a74a8f3dcc7f5a66f64d02dbde6e160ef98776c6fbcbf530b59d07",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "It's the official start of the third trimester — congratulations!",
        "text_sha256": "a577663e1384e4db476d21f85d185610a81d055788a972aa1958de62600e468e",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "You may not always feel like celebrating if you're dealing with common week 28 symptoms like back pain and sciatica . Hopefully, though, you're still fairly comfortable now that you're in month 7 of pregnancy.",
        "text_sha256": "19e5222f971f235f193eb4ae78ea6f6a9a8437d3cae577ac31b895ff1b3b2dd7",
        "word_count": 35
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Baby is getting more skilled by the day, and can now blink and even dream. And that's only the beginning ...",
        "text_sha256": "ebfd496b8217419ac508cec5efd771646c154fcfa922a33932ce998d60e209f2",
        "word_count": 21
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Your Baby at Week 28",
        "text_sha256": "d70db36380d23bff19527a32ea50d7f1c61f8b4aa59a7bd180d31d2d08d22d69",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "At a Glance",
        "text_sha256": "4007536f1ab858815b5f74377d1a44ff31bd2acc98e17bf65e9e39ed107102a1",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Your little dreamer",
        "text_sha256": "debb01e6d0ce5828735b05241194f0a22c87f54eb0e538c70bf0e8dd088ddb38",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Your baby begins to experience REM (rapid eye movement) sleep, which means it’s very likely your little one is dreaming!",
        "text_sha256": "bf7c1ef0319d6e103513004392dc7dfa5d1b091cf4aff08de680086ca9c5ba9d",
        "word_count": 20
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Baby can blink",
        "text_sha256": "ae81d643a330077ac1cb267891c40f45d3c76875039a847f571389b1dfc3a779",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "So far, your baby’s eyes have been shut tight. Now, your little sweetie can open and close those beautiful eyes, complete with brand new fluttering eyelashes.",
        "text_sha256": "4376ce99008484d1221588108c113606a33b77e1a4af548d25f293278758f882",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Making faces",
        "text_sha256": "3bced35c95f372c290bd3d50b8dd4b2022b32769b8d742c0581558d6cb75b708",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Fetuses often stick out their tongues at this age. No one is sure exactly why, but it’s possible that your baby is tasting your amniotic fluid.",
        "text_sha256": "b5ed24db6d78e6e64b449a9fb47cc17c74914e6e3fdd1249591f90a923ab0664",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "28 weeks pregnant is how many months?",
        "text_sha256": "170cc908cd8281aa4eb44d600409328fb4606ed17ff47d39f93fce4cbe25bf82",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you're 28 weeks pregnant, you're in month 7 of your pregnancy. Only 2 months left to go! Still have questions? Here's some more information on how weeks, months, and trimesters are broken down in pregnancy .",
        "text_sha256": "3165d0f7fe9c6c866df8ca384c287a1556fded101c346ae8a24e53dee3852f86",
        "word_count": 37
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "How big is my baby at 28 weeks?",
        "text_sha256": "a1810c5f7373b8ca0f29291fe0b8537e30b8439c968f9a7b8fae3d44f505d004",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Your little work-in-progress now weighs about 2¼ pounds and is almost 15 inches long when measured head to toe.",
        "text_sha256": "cf909d902003dc44e1796401d8d6da78bd2857286ba79a8e9a246306fccd7023",
        "word_count": 19
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Baby's getting into position",
        "text_sha256": "3c42e59ebbbf0cf3e1d011c25089248e657bf7588964751db6fc3964f82ff879",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Your baby is settling into the proper position for birth, which will be head-down toward your body's nearest exit!",
        "text_sha256": "1e41a739990ffb283c87fa12c2c4d4bfb1e1f8052631e6035cbc723ae1932882",
        "word_count": 19
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Baby is busy these days blinking — outside in the real world, blinking is necessary to help keep foreign objects out of the eyes. That skill is just one of an already impressive repertoire of tricks she's working on, like coughing, more intense sucking, hiccupping , and, perhaps most important, better breathing .",
        "text_sha256": "aa48bb3e7085ef7a64a5761a48437d0a3608a1067a731ec7b191b717f16341db",
        "word_count": 53
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Baby might be dreaming",
        "text_sha256": "b377cf045f8a9ae71bc6cb241a385efb38540db03bcf0fbd3f11d659c5594f48",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Dreaming about your baby at 28 weeks pregnant? Your baby may be dreaming about you too. Brain wave activity measured in a developing fetus shows different sleep cycles, including the rapid eye movement phase — the stage when dreaming occurs.",
        "text_sha256": "02631577077ad89139043795f0ccb1206554a02a1696c7aa6f88d57cc64d9087",
        "word_count": 40
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Your Body at Week 28",
        "text_sha256": "5a0a5a1d090a92a6c384fe65cdb4fac5f2033503faccc51c57459445a3070fd2",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Sciatica (tingling leg pain)",
        "text_sha256": "121b2b5b164d9672fbf139470d5546dc8a89ce2d509de684e92b752d02caf0af",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "This is it — at 28 weeks pregnant, you're two-thirds of the way to the finish line as you enter the third trimester . And what a difference a trimester makes!",
        "text_sha256": "3ee6d3034a0878a64b2d23ecf002ba42e33299da9634687c4bc37d2c93286b70",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Gone, most likely, are the days when you could call pregnancy \"comfortable\" — that is, if you ever did. Now, your baby's kicking may be keeping you up at night (or during the day), your feet may be swollen, you could be feeling more tired again, and your backache could be that pain that just won't quit.",
        "text_sha256": "dbc1aecea377b4199b2251b174b4dbe0e70a559a80584bbe0a922fece11caa45",
        "word_count": 57
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "And even though she hasn't started crying yet, it may seem like your baby's getting on your nerves already — literally. As she gets settled into position for birth, your little one's head and your growing uterus may rest on the sciatic nerve in the lower part of your spine.",
        "text_sha256": "b892c3d8ad01dbad10a63f8b96e6e20cc4d0bd26a5b9c63505b5e7a479158cce",
        "word_count": 50
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000027",
        "block_index": 27,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If that happens, you may feel sharp, shooting pain; tingling; or numbness that starts in your buttocks and radiates down the back of your legs — otherwise known as sciatica .",
        "text_sha256": "4aecd68c4dd2bf28025df8d1d556c59948db335697b3fc1c6d401f0bcb5ebe78",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000028",
        "block_index": 28,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The pain of sciatica can be quite intense at times, and though it may pass if your baby shifts positions, it can also linger until you've delivered.",
        "text_sha256": "aea3f92b8742e49921a6f6ec69ff3dde562fd1228f7b75a5094237c27e6e0680",
        "word_count": 27
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000029",
        "block_index": 29,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "A heating pad, warm bath, stretches, or just some self-imposed bed rest can help with the discomfort. So can pregnancy-approved physical therapy and some complementary and alternative therapies .",
        "text_sha256": "7a2c79d43aa221a17b573a5acd796fd8565f4f1ef18ca748b683ae501ba1cf9f",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000030",
        "block_index": 30,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Feeling sensitive (skin)?",
        "text_sha256": "79d53753a2a9acbb181b8ba3a3090f987977f45bb35ce95dff93fcd8fbc8c49b",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000031",
        "block_index": 31,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Sensitive skin can surface during pregnancy — even in someone who’s never had sensitive skin before. Some parts of the body may react because they’re dry and flaky, others because of heat rash or an external irritant, like the lotion you’ve been using for the past 10 years, which is suddenly driving you crazy.",
        "text_sha256": "6a31adc76db5e8dc431c25c7dc87dace5d32322f1c26628619b2fd4fdde8b5d5",
        "word_count": 54
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000032",
        "block_index": 32,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Typically the most sensitive spot is the belly, as it stretches. Other potential trouble spots include your hips and thighs.",
        "text_sha256": "0241454ec6355147de9f08b786086b0f48bcfa1d9bd487140ee1fcd570490ffa",
        "word_count": 20
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000033",
        "block_index": 33,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Your raging hormones make you more sensitive to contact with substances that might not normally affect you, such as sunlight, heat, detergents, chlorine, and even certain foods. And if you’ve got eczema , you can expect some major flare-ups — or if you’re very lucky, a nine-month respite.",
        "text_sha256": "35b7681fcaa49e1e839af60dc415116f830846777afda6942a102acfcb467e12",
        "word_count": 48
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000034",
        "block_index": 34,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "For itchy spots, a dab of calamine lotion should do the trick. If any rash or irritation lasts longer than a couple of days, ask your practitioner about next steps. Avoid products that are laden with tons of additives, dyes, or fragrance, any of which can exacerbate the problem.",
        "text_sha256": "2cef103a5dce13b01e8c449c23ba616270ea2321f31a519e12355fa6f630d141",
        "word_count": 49
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000035",
        "block_index": 35,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Pregnancy Symptoms Week 28",
        "text_sha256": "c524f3ced329fb2df559c44dc31a1d0c18f3f21965cf65af65015fbfce9153bb",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000036",
        "block_index": 36,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Bloating and gas",
        "text_sha256": "ba6a7b566d08ead069fdc80bf3cb2123647c09d6797ae086b5330bb38a853021",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000037",
        "block_index": 37,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Your growing uterus may be putting extra pressure on your rectum, causing you to lose some control over the muscles in your rear. Add your sluggish digestive system to the equation — thanks to pregnancy hormones that relax intestinal muscles — and you may find that you’re particularly gassy. Try to eat six small meals a day instead of three large ones so you don’t overtax your digestive system.",
        "text_sha256": "4d50fd576c838148c927006e80d3e89028aa4471cb7409b1f2b7979a06066b71",
        "word_count": 69
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000038",
        "block_index": 38,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Stuffy nose",
        "text_sha256": "6aac0cfc04aee92dc67a3d788ccdc23ebc4b2408d1ae86bde2d744c6c1450005",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000039",
        "block_index": 39,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "High levels of estrogen and progesterone increase blood flow to the mucus membranes in your nose, causing them to swell. If your stuffy nose is making it hard for you to breathe at night — or making you snore — try wearing a nasal strip at bedtime to open up your nostrils.",
        "text_sha256": "5b5471ee16c94168e9ad896a2857911e9f5c19dad367e8614cf435b1266292ea",
        "word_count": 52
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000040",
        "block_index": 40,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Faintness or dizziness",
        "text_sha256": "5313011634ace64e276a3554f3a6033770c6a2bdb65dd49ce7f9f4f940a23857",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000041",
        "block_index": 41,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you thought your days of feeling light-headed were over after your first trimester, think again. For some women, that bulging belly puts pressure on blood vessels, which reduces blood flow to the brain and can cause dizziness. Keep blood circulating and pumping to your brain by drinking plenty of water each day.",
        "text_sha256": "f7347056291b6eb07a3f15b6f3b99b8a56a79d5b08e2a10e0c14df1ce9b1b62c",
        "word_count": 53
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000042",
        "block_index": 42,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Symphysis pubis dysfunction (SPD)",
        "text_sha256": "0044a4244d0bd5ee25ada9536283e3efd06820f0d7ec41a3b85695c59fab9cfc",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000043",
        "block_index": 43,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "This weird pregnancy symptom develops when the hormone relaxin makes the ligaments in your pelvic joint too relaxed and stretchy, causing the pelvic joint to become unstable. If it's painful, ask your practitioner about wearing a pelvic support belt, available online, which stabilizes the ligaments and helps keep the pelvic joint in place.",
        "text_sha256": "fe1dc96f1c201df6d4445e61f480bc118a34946ae2bcff42ba341f4a425a3db6",
        "word_count": 53
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000044",
        "block_index": 44,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Bleeding gums",
        "text_sha256": "3f189a5230f4bc8f637104d797dba7330408856782b0ab3582db45a5d86893eb",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000045",
        "block_index": 45,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Inflamed and irritated gums are quite common during pregnancy, since ramped-up hormones may cause gums to swell and leave your mouth more vulnerable to bacteria and plaque. When you brush your teeth, remember to brush your tongue to minimize the amount of bacteria in your mouth.",
        "text_sha256": "55e8c2299717b150067c9288fd0a68fd97982b38e5a4017f9b8a7e9d6d45eb85",
        "word_count": 46
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000046",
        "block_index": 46,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Mask of pregnancy (melasma)",
        "text_sha256": "bcd8f85f85a06f185bbac448d2b8c3f356e134a51e17bfbe62f8f987d9b7ab9f",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000047",
        "block_index": 47,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Pregnancy hormones can cause hyperpigmentation of the skin — particularly if you have a darker complexion to begin with. This can result in pronounced freckles or moles, a dark line down the center of your tummy (linea nigra), or dark or brown patches on your face called melasma. Don’t worry — most discolorations fade a few months after giving birth. Since sunlight can intensify hyperpigmentation, try to stay in the shade and put on sunscreen with an SPF of 30 or more.",
        "text_sha256": "5f001d7ee546f28d912c99f059a806e37c9ba0af455ae11bea525eba91282574",
        "word_count": 82
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000048",
        "block_index": 48,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Tips for You This Week",
        "text_sha256": "32770aa6fb9708009741b1a7b10691529ec1e23f79116914a353fdf3f2baf4e7",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000049",
        "block_index": 49,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Start doing kick counts",
        "text_sha256": "fd6118fdf0e747bbdbe630285b3da7dabe08e93971770cb87ada7e0b01382e25",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000050",
        "block_index": 50,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Beginning in week 28, doctors recommend that you start monitoring baby’s movement by doing kick counts .",
        "text_sha256": "f57abfd5dd93391ba32b6c38b48633e42a709c9edcedffc53885170174fcd576",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000051",
        "block_index": 51,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Kick counts are just what they sound like — you’ll count the kicks, taps, flutters, or rolls you feel during a specific period of time.",
        "text_sha256": "2dd0e8ebd1ec408c5044b063d0de230a445218cc18e18e41456ef7687669dc0f",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000052",
        "block_index": 52,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "During the third trimester , you should usually feel 10 movements within about two hours, though every pregnancy is different. A good time to do them is whenever you feel your baby moving , like after a meal or early in the morning.",
        "text_sha256": "9eb200ab298e2c7bfca628320b8bf610e96d89d105e235f9ec0e7217a25099b4",
        "word_count": 43
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000053",
        "block_index": 53,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "During the third trimester , you should usually feel 10 movements within about two hours, though every pregnancy is different. A good time to do them is whenever you",
        "text_sha256": "84221c3d58eb404241bb4d237851c7014f24c37e0aec2475b88afa5fceec4d84",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000054",
        "block_index": 54,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": ", like after a meal or early in the morning.",
        "text_sha256": "22e959f980a4c41b3f311f5b5dd0b95e25c7328ff68678b1f4cd98255bd55f0b",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000055",
        "block_index": 55,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "First, remove any distractions around you and note the time you started. Then, put your hands on your belly and start to count any movements you feel. Once you arrive at 10 movements, write down the end time.",
        "text_sha256": "0083a51b568d9dbbb43119bf21c066cb0c182bb0aa82695bb5456244235a4280",
        "word_count": 38
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000056",
        "block_index": 56,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you don’t notice 10 movements within a two-hour period, call your doctor, who may want to do a quick check-up. Just know that in time, you’ll get a good sense of your baby’s kick patterns and how things are going in there.",
        "text_sha256": "6f206449efb5d98373f8e87ddf237377fcebe935db8efa2e7dc243c75b7fa35a",
        "word_count": 43
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000057",
        "block_index": 57,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Remember, though, that if there's a noticeable decrease in your baby's movements , call the doctor or head to an urgent care or hospital right away.",
        "text_sha256": "90dea5faee44db402bddf21e8c15754687e5d25d58e5802be8b9450056940602",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000058",
        "block_index": 58,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Find out your Rh status",
        "text_sha256": "5ee2a93263ebc37f69f67f3911f8dc7ff20117625a9c99d4f1e8aef7bdba656c",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000059",
        "block_index": 59,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Do you know if you're Rh positive or Rh negative? If not, it’s important to find out.",
        "text_sha256": "ffd68a23746e63605805bec20dc80d83f599cfa38662130a9fa97956775cf5cf",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000060",
        "block_index": 60,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The Rh factor is a protein found in most people's red blood cells. If you have it, you're Rh positive; if you don't have it, you're Rh negative.",
        "text_sha256": "d63f27909caa8a6211cb9f7ba3ab78d2cec54dd382fe6bf3f67f40efedb88fad",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000061",
        "block_index": 61,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "is a protein found in most people's red blood cells. If you have it, you're Rh positive; if you don't have it, you're Rh negative.",
        "text_sha256": "c624934aff7594650d60f6bcabd01c9a7e3cf1b7fbfa03fdb57e91c5bf11f20e",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000062",
        "block_index": 62,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Unless you're pregnant, your status usually doesn't matter much, but problems can occur if, for example, you're Rh negative and your baby is Rh positive.",
        "text_sha256": "673a59a34f8e7e3d1e013c30886d56d703b6567f454860dd9d12e9eaca0c24c3",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000063",
        "block_index": 63,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "In the case of Rh incompatibility, your immune system may view your baby's blood cells as \"foreign\" substances and mobilize an army of antibodies to attack them.",
        "text_sha256": "17412c4340bf275dfa5c5d00d2a3ff4835f6866c9f8ea9d2e7f6a249752ac02f",
        "word_count": 27
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000064",
        "block_index": 64,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you are Rh negative and your baby is Rh positive, you’ll need a vaccine-like injection of Rh-immune globulin this week, known as RhoGAM , to prevent the development of antibodies.",
        "text_sha256": "682c85ce6bb807edb2d36bca8582d9403fee0e7368b040aad929d832de81469f",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000065",
        "block_index": 65,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Ask about breast changes",
        "text_sha256": "c1fdfc1ae856dc902ee5f04a020d3d9ea35f4f5a692ff42f0521e9bd0874710d",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000066",
        "block_index": 66,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Though finding a breast lump during pregnancy can be scary, rest assured it’s more than likely nothing to worry about.",
        "text_sha256": "e7147e662e2c6868cb29cdb3455f7e59e7697fb2bbe360c0b9937ee66229c61f",
        "word_count": 20
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000067",
        "block_index": 67,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "can be scary, rest assured it’s more than likely nothing to worry about.",
        "text_sha256": "31a6dd0a169a13fa21224963d6372c8554cd1255c8ef269162737ae605d03c57",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000068",
        "block_index": 68,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Having breast cancer during pregnancy is very rare, especially if you’re under 35, according to the American Cancer Society (ACS) — plus the many changes that are happening to your breasts while you’re expecting can cause them to feel much more lumpy, heavy, and firm than you’re used to.",
        "text_sha256": "0c130d04622798e57f304858f6269ba15f9112ab93d9768cb02372348ebdecdb",
        "word_count": 49
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000069",
        "block_index": 69,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "while you’re expecting can cause them to feel much more lumpy, heavy, and firm than you’re used to.",
        "text_sha256": "bcc4af796806f7f57d5266c61a3cb3990c5d4660fc852bdf61457c282921329c",
        "word_count": 18
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000070",
        "block_index": 70,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Tender lumps are common during the third trimester, but still, they shouldn’t be ignored. Ask your provider for a breast exam at your next checkup.",
        "text_sha256": "37f583e7e24fd4183ebb7f4b9f743e1d8077f0ce47700f25ed487f13ef74371a",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000071",
        "block_index": 71,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Up your iron",
        "text_sha256": "d74fdad55077737746316063c41e493589af49efdbba68f9122b8cab61787a4b",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000072",
        "block_index": 72,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Babies absorb the majority of their iron stores during the third trimester, so nosh on iron-rich foods like chicken, beans, spinach, tofu, beef, and enriched cereals.",
        "text_sha256": "15760521bb8f1beb25da657df7b3a57344f74da254345d6300a6fbe5b5911e8c",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000073",
        "block_index": 73,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Apart from Popeye, vitamin C is iron's best bud since it can improve iron absorption . So take a glass of OJ with that iron supplement during pregnancy, a side of red pepper with those shrimp, or some fresh strawberries in your oat bran cereal.",
        "text_sha256": "1f6518e906d58b73906c573ca517f246c0b0d86809f987de6d1cf3ead853ea3c",
        "word_count": 45
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000074",
        "block_index": 74,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Schedule your Tdap vaccine",
        "text_sha256": "99f60efb40c4fca237f0775329573d47c01619e837a4485edbe4986b36a045a2",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000075",
        "block_index": 75,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Getting the Tdap vaccine when you're pregnant is not only safe, it's smart. Tdap — short for tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis — protects your baby from whooping cough, which can be very dangerous for newborns.",
        "text_sha256": "1f6250ad8d004e1d930cb3dccf7b7b9f9972184ce025c89ca26ffb6e8d17f59d",
        "word_count": 35
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000076",
        "block_index": 76,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "when you're pregnant is not only safe, it's smart. Tdap — short for tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis — protects your baby from whooping cough, which can be very dangerous for newborns.",
        "text_sha256": "b00ff85655766d1aae78cd71a69998d3f4485f14812e1133865235225631aad6",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000077",
        "block_index": 77,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "When you roll up your sleeve, your vaccine passes antibodies to your baby, providing protection until your infant is ready for a DTaP shot at 2 months. If you haven’t had a flu shot , now’s the time to get one of those too.",
        "text_sha256": "0248e31913e78bac7f73acbb04fd389a2a95ca1021fc2d1dca7a0c46a0e36e97",
        "word_count": 44
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000078",
        "block_index": 78,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Choosing a childbirth class",
        "text_sha256": "2ce1838b39413f94b0dae52f2496c74b5aa49e3aca53a49f3062e6982b3c9625",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000079",
        "block_index": 79,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Now is a good time to research childbirth classes . You can choose a class at the hospital, with a local instructor, or via a teacher online.",
        "text_sha256": "21e939ca8f52c3d0b464879c5d89821e01d96c2dd07677507aaba1755e2e55d0",
        "word_count": 27
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000080",
        "block_index": 80,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": ". You can choose a class at the hospital, with a local instructor, or via a teacher online.",
        "text_sha256": "2e76f0afa50ac39ce0dc0856590b609994554c95172de678b14e81c6afee3eb1",
        "word_count": 18
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000081",
        "block_index": 81,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Just make sure you sign up early so you can finish several weeks before your due date. Ask whether your course includes lessons on infant care, CPR , and breastfeeding (it should).",
        "text_sha256": "bb1eec41c6478913b6d3f966bc5bb0c61b08672e02ef735fc8aeab9c7a9663ab",
        "word_count": 32
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000082",
        "block_index": 82,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Just make sure you sign up early so you can finish several weeks before your due date. Ask whether your course includes lessons on infant care,",
        "text_sha256": "35ab8937c64c26b8c030808c7f4dc7c00bda552a980ea4ab48f5ccc2b4ad8c96",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000083",
        "block_index": 83,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Have special requirements? There are classes for second-timers who need to brush up on their techniques, courses for moms attempting a vaginal birth after cesarean (VBAC) , and classes designed for those expecting multiples .",
        "text_sha256": "a9e21a8c604a4e39e5581207e9e80403ee16c052e3839463a59d94b5c6b6b88a",
        "word_count": 35
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000084",
        "block_index": 84,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Whichever type you choose, make sure your instructor is certified by a national childbirth education organization. And here's a bonus: Your insurance company may cover your tuition, so be sure to submit your bill.",
        "text_sha256": "09351686f307a79defc47cf76ae9de65522a8d4997ba3f3d09eccaf4a9c66384",
        "word_count": 34
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000085",
        "block_index": 85,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Have the circumcision talk",
        "text_sha256": "69a10f8881b889550809d6d7998e765ccffa657c8126b5a4c8a8a5d87a142847",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000086",
        "block_index": 86,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Before you got pregnant, you may not have thought too much about whether or not to circumcise a baby boy if you had one. But if you've got a son on the way, it's a decision you'll have to make — and it may be a tricky one if you don’t have religious or cultural traditions guiding you.",
        "text_sha256": "2d5f28fc08dda456661ff2b3df9396767b2fd4ebcb84e95848017c6d52564a9f",
        "word_count": 58
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000087",
        "block_index": 87,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "if you had one. But if you've got a son on the way, it's a decision you'll have to make — and it may be a tricky one if you don’t have religious or cultural traditions guiding you.",
        "text_sha256": "149786c821ad9e09a4d5a7126e11c992e9f8c17781e525aa4224937607e1e787",
        "word_count": 38
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000088",
        "block_index": 88,
        "block_type": "p",
